<header><p class="st-kicker">county · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Mâcon</h1><p class="st-meta">850 CE – 1239 CE (approx.) · capital Mâcon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Carolingian county in southern Burgundy, the land in which the great abbey of Cluny was founded in 910.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Mâconnais, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macon">Mâcon</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saone">Saône</a>, became a Carolingian county in the 9th century, at the junction of the lands of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/west-francia">West Francia</a> and the Burgundian kingdoms. Its early counts were linked with the dukes of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-aquitaine">Aquitaine</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In 910 Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-i-duke-of-aquitaine">William I of Aquitaine</a> founded the abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cluny-abbey">Cluny</a> in the county, free from lay and episcopal control, and it became the head of a vast monastic network. From the late 10th century the county was held by a branch of the house of Burgundy-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivrea">Ivrea</a> descended from Otto-William, who also ruled the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-county-of-burgundy">Free County of Burgundy</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The last countess, Alix, and her husband John of Dreux sold the county to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a> in 1239, and it was attached to the royal domain. The Mâconnais remains known for its wines.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 850 CE – 1239 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-